# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Terraform
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/.terraform/*
.terraform.lock.hcl.bak

# State files MUST never be committed - they contain plaintext secrets
# (e.g. AlloyDB initial_user password) and infrastructure inventory.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfstate.backup
crash.log
crash.*.log

# Variable files frequently contain project IDs, CIDRs and secrets.
# Commit only *.tfvars.example - never the real thing.
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
!*.tfvars.example
!*.auto.tfvars.example

# CLI config / plan output
.terraformrc
terraform.rc
*.tfplan
*.tfplan.json
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Credentials & secrets - defence in depth, these should never exist locally
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.json.key
*-sa-key.json
service-account*.json
application_default_credentials.json
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors / OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python / tooling scratch
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.tflint.d/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local research notes
#
# .research/ holds the raw evidence behind the claims in this repo: API dumps
# of supported database flags and metric descriptors, plus the curated
# VERIFIED_FACTS.md. It is working material rather than part of what we publish,
# so it stays local. See .research/README.md for how to regenerate it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.research/
